                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "SPOILERS AHAED, DONT SCROLL, ILL DISTRACT YOU\r\nA\r\nA\r\nA\r\nA\r\nA\r\nA\r\nA\r\nA\r\nA\r\nA\r\n\r\nA\r\nA\r\nA\r\nA\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nwhat did uchikoshi mean by this\r\nabsolute peak\r\n\r\nUnironically though i really liked this game. I hated the puzzles for the most part, might be a skill issue, but I REALLY hated them.\r\n\r\nThe story is... fucking weird, cinema, weird, peak, all of the above, and even more. I dont fucking know what this game is telling me but I liked it.\r\n\r\nThe plot twists made me lose my fucking mind, this might be the most crackhead Uchikoshi ever holy shit, the final act was fucking insane.\r\n\r\nThe structure, is obviously, messy as all fuck. Dunno how it would work otherwise.\r\n\r\nThe animation was beautiful, shut up.\r\nD team was REALLY well written and I mean REALLY well written holy fucking shit.\r\nQ Team is actual ragebait what the hell were they even cooking??? Mira went nowhere, and Eric just fucking trauma dumped, didn't get over it, then they threw a trial, exposition dumped him, and called it a day lmfao.\r\nC Team was... I... uh.... Carlos.... just.... Carlos...... mmmfgh\r\n\r\nI think the villain is really fucking good in the weirdest way, this guy is the most dumb genius ever.\r\n\r\nIf I would have to actually describe what I thought the game was telling me was basically just to believe in faith, hope, love, and luck.\r\n\r\nBefore I end I have to say the fucking Diana & Sigma ending was insanely good, best moment in this game by far.",
